 // ## Pre-release Version Identifier
 // A numeric identifier, or a non-numeric identifier.
+// The non-numeric form is tried first.  Both alternatives accept a
+// disjoint set of identifiers, so this only changes which one is
+// reached when the numeric form could match a proper prefix of the
+// identifier (eg the `7` of `7f3c`).  Anchored consumers backtrack to
+// the same result either way, but unanchored ones (COERCEFULL) would
+// otherwise stop at that prefix whenever the terminus check, which
+// only rejects digits, let a following letter through.
 
-createToken('PRERELEASEIDENTIFIER', `(?:${src[t.NUMERICIDENTIFIER]
-}|${src[t.NONNUMERICIDENTIFIER]})`)
+createToken('PRERELEASEIDENTIFIER', `(?:${src[t.NONNUMERICIDENTIFIER]
+}|${src[t.NUMERICIDENTIFIER]})`)
 
 createToken('PRERELEASEIDENTIFIERLOOSE', `(?:${src[t.NUMERICIDENTIFIERLOOSE]
 }|${src[t.NONNUMERICIDENTIFIER]})`)
